.TH AMP 1 "November 2026" "animated-man-page" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amp \- animated man page pager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amp
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-install\-hint ]
.RB [ \-\-cleanup\-hint ]
.RI [ file ]
.P
.B man \-P
.I /path/to/amp/amp
.I topic
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amp
(short for
.IR "animated man page" )
is a terminal pager similar in spirit to
.BR less (1).
It displays formatted manual-page text and can overlay live animations
inside rectangular regions marked in the document.
.P
It is intended to be used as
.B MANPAGER
(or via
.BR man (1)'s
.B \-P
option) so that selected pages can show a typescript or caca-style
animation while the surrounding documentation remains readable.
.P
This content best viewed with
.BR amp .
.SS Animation box (preferred)
An animation region is a
.I box
delimited by markers.  Between the markers you put
.B static
lines that ordinary pagers (
.BR less ,
.BR more )
will show unchanged.  When the page is viewed with
.BR amp ,
those lines are overwritten by the live animation.
.P
Up to five boxes are supported.
.P
Format:
.EX
<<<ANIM_BOX w=\fIW\fR h=\fIH\fR id=\fIL\fR timing=\fIfile\fR typescript=\fIfile\fR>>>
    static line 1 (visible in less / more)
    static line 2
    \.\.\.
<<<END_ANIM_BOX>>>
.EE
.P
Attributes (space-separated
.BR key = value
pairs; values may be quoted):
.TP
.B w=\fIN\fR
Box width in columns (recommended).
.TP
.B h=\fIN\fR
Box height in rows (recommended).  amp reads up to
.I N
lines of static body (or until
.BR END_ANIM_BOX ).
.TP
.B id=\fIL\fR
Single letter A–Z identifying this region (default: first free letter).
Used when resolving
.B ANIM_L_*
environment variables if paths are not given on the marker.
.TP
.B timing=\fIpath\fR
.BR script (1)
timing file for this box.  Absolute path, path relative to the current
directory, or a basename looked up under the data directories listed in
.BR FILES .
.TP
.B typescript=\fIpath\fR
Corresponding typescript file (same path rules as
.BR timing ).
.TP
.B divisor=\fIN\fR
Speed multiplier for
.BR scriptreplay (1)
(default 1.0).
.TP
.B loop=\fI0\fR|\fI1\fR
Whether the animation loops (default 1).
.P
Marker lines are removed from the display under amp.  The static body is
blanked and replaced by the animation so no residue remains.
.P
Example with two boxes (paths relative to a data directory – see
.BR FILES ):
.EX
This content best viewed with amp.

<<<ANIM_BOX w=40 h=8 id=A timing=demo.timing typescript=demo.typescript>>>
    [ Animation A – demo session ]
    [ Shown here when not using amp ]
<<<END_ANIM_BOX>>>

<<<ANIM_BOX w=24 h=6 id=B timing=b.timing typescript=b.typescript>>>
    [ Animation B placeholder ]
<<<END_ANIM_BOX>>>
.EE
.SS Legacy letter filler
Solid runs of at least eight identical uppercase letters (and at least two
rows) still mark a region and map to
.B ANIM_L_TIMING
/
.B ANIM_L_TYPESCRIPT
when no marker paths are present.  Prefer the explicit
.B ANIM_BOX
form for new pages.
.SS Animation source resolution
For each box, timing and typescript paths are taken from, in order:
.IP 1. 3
.B timing=
and
.B typescript=
attributes on the
.B ANIM_BOX
line (preferred – no environment variables required);
.IP 2. 3
environment
.B ANIM_L_TIMING
and
.B ANIM_L_TYPESCRIPT
(where
.I L
is the box
.BR id );
.IP 3. 3
legacy
.B ANIM_TIMING
/
.B ANIM_TYPESCRIPT
for id
.B Q
only.
.P
When the marker supplies both paths, only
.B MANPAGER
needs to be set; the
.B ANIM_*
variables are optional.
.P
Path values may be quoted (single or double quotes) or unquoted.
Absolute paths and paths containing
.B ~
are accepted.
Relative names are resolved in this order:
.IP 1. 3
as given (current working directory);
.IP 2. 3
.I $AMP_DATA_DIR/
and
.I $AMP_DATA_DIR/animations/ ;
.IP 3. 3
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/amp/
and
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/amp/animations/ ;
.IP 4. 3
.I ~/.local/share/amp/
and
.I ~/.local/share/amp/animations/ ;
.IP 5. 3
.I /usr/share/amp/
and
.I /usr/share/amp/animations/ .
.P
Animations
.B loop by default.
If no usable files are found, a coloured spinner is shown in the box
instead.  Prepare typescripts with
.BR amp\-trim (1)
so clear-screen sequences are removed and the content fits the box.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a terse usage summary and install/uninstall pointers, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-hint
Print short install/uninstall summary.
.TP
.B \-\-cleanup\-hint
Point at
.BR uninstall.sh .
.TP
.I file
Optional path to a pre-formatted text file.  When omitted,
.B amp
reads standard input (the normal case when invoked by
.BR man (1)).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANPAGER
Set to the
.B amp
wrapper script so
.BR man (1)
uses amp as its pager.
.TP
.B AMP_DATA_DIR
Preferred directory for animation timing/typescript files.  Checked first
when resolving relative paths from
.B ANIM_BOX
attributes.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
If set,
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/amp
is searched after
.BR AMP_DATA_DIR .
.TP
.B ANIM_L_TIMING / ANIM_L_TYPESCRIPT
Fallback paths for box id
.I L
when the marker does not supply them.
.TP
.B ANIM_L_DIVISOR / ANIM_L_LOOP
Optional speed and loop controls for id
.IR L .
.TP
.B ANIM_TIMING / ANIM_TYPESCRIPT / ANIM_DIVISOR
Legacy aliases for id
.B Q
only.
.SH FILES
Animation files are resolved in this order for relative names:
.TP
.I $AMP_DATA_DIR/
.TQ
.I $AMP_DATA_DIR/animations/
Explicit override (highest priority after absolute paths and
.IR ./ ).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/amp/
.TQ
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/amp/animations/
Per-user data (default
.I XDG_DATA_HOME
is
.IR ~/.local/share ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/amp/
.TQ
.I ~/.local/share/amp/animations/
Default user location when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amp/
.TQ
.I /usr/share/amp/animations/
System-wide location for packaged animations.
.P
Recommended layout for a small collection:
.EX
~/.local/share/amp/animations/
    demo.timing
    demo.typescript
    b.timing
    b.typescript
.EE
.P
Then a man page can use short names:
.EX
<<<ANIM_BOX w=40 h=8 id=A timing=demo.timing typescript=demo.typescript>>>
.EE
.SH KEYS
.TS
lb l.
q	Quit
space / PgDn	Page forward
b / PgUp	Page backward
j / ↓	Line forward
k / ↑	Line backward
g / Home	Go to top
G / End	Go to bottom
/	Start search
n / N	Next / previous match
h / ?	Help screen (animation paused)
.TE
.SH INSTALLATION
The recommended wrapper is the
.B amp
script next to
.B amp.py
(avoids quoting issues with
.BR man (1)).
.P
One-shot:
.EX
man -P /path/to/amp/amp ls
.EE
.P
Session-only:
.EX
export MANPAGER=/path/to/amp/amp
man ls
.EE
.P
Permanent (bash/zsh):
.EX
echo 'export MANPAGER=/path/to/amp/amp' >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
.EE
.P
Helper scripts:
.EX
./install.sh              # show the export line
./install.sh --permanent  # append to the shell rc file
./uninstall.sh            # reverse the above
.EE
.P
A controlling terminal (/dev/tty) is required.
.SH CLEANUP
.EX
unset MANPAGER
unset ANIM_A_TIMING ANIM_A_TYPESCRIPT ANIM_A_DIVISOR ANIM_A_LOOP
./uninstall.sh
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Empty input when content was expected.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, missing file, or no controlling terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# view a local page with paths on the ANIM_BOX line
python3 amp.py sample_man.txt

# or resolve short names from the user data dir
mkdir -p ~/.local/share/amp/animations
cp demo.timing demo.typescript ~/.local/share/amp/animations/
man -P ./amp some-animated-page
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amp\-trim (1),
.BR man (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR script (1),
.BR scriptreplay (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Animated man-page demo
